-- glucose: the anomeric exchange, whose rate is the amount of hydroxide dissolved. Tag 1 is hydroxide, and
-- the base rate is zero: in water alone the exchange runs at 2.5 x 10^-4 per second, which is an order of
-- magnitude of nothing, and each order of magnitude of base buys an order of magnitude of rate.
m-glucose : Material
m-glucose = (2 , cons (nat-xch (cons 0 nil) (cons 1 nil) , brate-catalysed 1 0 , true) nil , cons 0 (cons 1 nil))
